From: gts9wifi Fedora port
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: lpass-va-macro: wire SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS

In Linux 7.3 lpass-va-macro uses pm_clk_suspend()/pm_clk_resume() for
runtime PM (releasing macro/dcodec Q6PRM votes), but still lacks
SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS so forced system suspend can leave the clocks
enabled.  Wire pm_runtime_force_suspend/resume as SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS.

---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
@@ -1755,6 +1755,7 @@ static int va_macro_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops va_macro_pm_ops = {
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(va_macro_runtime_suspend, va_macro_runtime_resume, NULL)
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id va_macro_dt_match[] = {
